{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/713860-which-mokole-building-method-do-you-prefer-set-in-stone-or-fluctuating-by-gnosis","id":713860,"title":"Which Mokole building method do you prefer: set in stone or fluctuating by Gnosis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-22T00:26:47-07:00","id":713860,"title":"Which Mokole building method do you prefer: set in stone or fluctuating by Gnosis","content":"I know that in the old version that once you had your dragon form, it was set in stone. I believe this changed somewhat with the W20 Changing Breeds, and that it all depends on what your current Gnosis score is. I like both versions, but sort of liked the first one more, as this added a wild-card dimension with some Mokole, especially reptile born, being &quot;special&quot; and others less so. What are your thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T08:14:51-07:00","id":714596,"title":"","content":"From a gm stand point I like the newer version, because it puts less pressure on my players to start a game with a 10 gnosis or to fight the GM for it. I've noticed a calmer player character creation for mokol\u00e8.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T09:22:58-07:00","id":714686,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify: It's still the permanent score that counts, only no longer the one you had at the beginning of the game.<br /> <br /> And I really, really like that. One of the things that draw people to playing Mokole is that you can heavily customize your Archid form (even though I'm a little sad the additional limbs are no longer supported...). Making this dependent only on starting gnosis means everyone will put as many freebies into this stat as possible and probably start as Suchid as well, whether it makes sense for the character concept or not, because not doing so gets punished like almost nothing else in the system. It's a little like saying &quot;We're playing Core Werewolf, but only Red Talons can switch to Crinos. Everyone else has to buy a 7 point merit if they want to do so. Now, what tribes do you choose?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T06:46:31-07:00","id":744337,"title":"","content":"Question: is the natural unhenanced state of the Archid as a quadruped without grasping hands? Do you have to take traits for that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T09:21:49-07:00","id":744593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vidyaraja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/713860-which-mokole-building-method-do-you-prefer-set-in-stone-or-fluctuating-by-gnosis?p=744337#post744337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: is the natural unhenanced state of the Archid as a quadruped without grasping hands? Do you have to take traits for that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Natural state for an Archid is quadruped if you don't take &quot;Upright Walking&quot;, grasping hands is extra. I always rule it in my game that if you take &quot;upright walking&quot; you can grasp items, and need grasping hands for anything more dexterous then to hold and use a weapon. I think forcing someone to buy both just so they can use their Blade of the Kings is a little harsh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T09:22:22-07:00","id":744595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cifer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/713860-which-mokole-building-method-do-you-prefer-set-in-stone-or-fluctuating-by-gnosis?p=714686#post714686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify: It's still the permanent score that counts, only no longer the one you had at the beginning of the game.<br /> <br /> And I really, really like that. One of the things that draw people to playing Mokole is that you can heavily customize your Archid form (even though I'm a little sad the additional limbs are no longer supported...). Making this dependent only on starting gnosis means everyone will put as many freebies into this stat as possible and probably start as Suchid as well, whether it makes sense for the character concept or not, because not doing so gets punished like almost nothing else in the system. It's a little like saying &quot;We're playing Core Werewolf, but only Red Talons can switch to Crinos. Everyone else has to buy a 7 point merit if they want to do so. Now, what tribes do you choose?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly my thoughts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T13:58:41-07:00","id":745047,"title":"","content":"I get it, I just like the idea; as NPCs, that some of the mysterious dragon folk make the others look pale by comparison. Sort of Sidhe vs Commoner, or True Fae vs Changeling. Most of the dragons are comparable to a scaly Crinos, and a few are born DRAGONS. It's like Pure Breed, but with more substantial privelege attached to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T14:52:04-07:00","id":745173,"title":"","content":"Well, as NPCs, it's pretty simple: The scaly Crinos guys don't have a vast pile of Gnosis, the dragon guys do. Whether raising Gnosis is something that everyone can do has never been described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T19:13:52-07:00","id":745554,"title":"","content":"Exactly, not every garou has a 10 gnosis, not every mokole will either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T19:14:25-07:00","id":745556,"title":"","content":"even over the course of their lifetime","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-31T22:38:53-07:00","id":745835,"title":"","content":"To some extent, I think the process of gaining a form is dramatic enough to not just throw new traits on.<br /> <br /> However, min/maxing aspect did really need to go.<br /> <br /> I would go with allowing characters to enhance their form. (An extra Huge Size, \u200bas the character literally grows. 'Learning' to grab things with his tail, etc.)<br /> <br /> Now if they really want major changes, that would require a trip to Flux or a relevant dream realm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}